    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <p class="pencil-label">Hollis Ouellette</p>
      <h1 class="title-page mt-3 text-[clamp(2.25rem,2.6vw+1rem,3.5rem)] leading-[1.1]">I learned to write on deadline. I learned to write slowly much later.</h1>
      <p class="body-copy mt-7">I was born in Winooski, across the river from Burlington, where my grandparents had come down from Quebec to work in the mills. I spent fourteen years at daily papers in Maine and Vermont, writing features and a weekly column. In 2019 I left, and for six years I taught the personal essay in a college&rsquo;s evening program.</p>
      <p class="body-copy mt-4">The first cohort of The Slow Draft was six people on Zoom in January 2021, from my kitchen table. I have taught it fifteen times now. My own essays are in <i class="serif">The Lower Falls</i>.</p>
